One canonical rule source rendered into each harness's native surface, killing the
duplicated hand-authored Cursor generators and the drifting .claude/rules/workflow.md
copy. Rules are thin pointers (content parity via AGENTS.md projection), not always-on
policy bodies duplicated per harness.

- rules/: single canonical source (workflow, tdd, security, documentation) as THIN
  pointers to AGENTS.md + stage skills — no 100-line policy bodies.
- lib/rules-sync.js: renders Cursor .cursor/rules/*.mdc from the canonical source (the
  only harness with a first-class native rule surface). Claude/Codex/Hermes receive the
  same policy through their AGENTS.md instruction projection — no always-on token bloat.
- lib/agents-config.js: generateCursorConfig now derives from rules-sync; deleted the
  hardcoded generateCursorWorkflow/Tdd/Security/Documentation duplicates.
- Drop deprecated .cursorrules emission: cursor.plugin.json rootConfig removed, committed
  file deleted, protected-surfaces list updated, legacy-file cleanup added to setup.
  Cursor detection (detect-agent) is kept.
- setup.js: Claude no longer copies always-on rule files (uses AGENTS.md); removed the
  copyAgentRules mechanism.
- Drift enforcement (no committed .claude/.cursor/.hermes mirrors; .codex/skills stays
  the committed sentinel): rules use a regenerate-into-temp determinism gate; skills add
  an all-four-harness render round-trip (test/structural/*).
- Hermes: added to HARNESS_IDS + every capability row (CLI-consumed model); reconciled
  docs/reference/AGENT_SKILL_PARITY.md ("Hermes support is planned" was false).
- Fixed stage-graph contradiction: removed the .claude/commands command shim (commands
  were removed in A0d) and corrected stale parity-doc lines (Cursor "unproven", Claude
  "command-first", .claude/commands shim vs commands: removed).
- lib/mcp-config-renderer.js: generic per-harness MCP renderer (read->merge->write,
  idempotent) fixing setup's .mcp.json skip-if-exists bug; frozen descriptor
  {name, transport, command, args, envRefs} with ${VAR} env references only.
- Regenerated the D20 bd call-site kill-list artifact (line-number shifts).

Refs: agent-rules parity audit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
